style/data/emotions/emotions.tsv and style/data/hidden-verbs/nominalizations.tsv
are derived from Princeton WordNet 3.0 (https://wordnet.princeton.edu/), release
tarball WordNet-3.0.tar.gz (sha256
640db279c949a88f61f851dd54ebbb22d003f8b90b85267042ef85a3781d3a52). WordNet 3.0
Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights reserved. They are used and
modified under the WordNet License, whose full text, including the disclaimer,
is in style/data/licenses/WordNet-LICENSE; the tables are not licensed MIT OR
Apache-2.0. emotions.tsv, modified by writemorebetter: single-word lemmas of
the noun.feeling synsets and the hyponyms of feeling.n.01 and emotion.n.01,
adjectives derived from or attributes of those nouns and their satellites, and verbs whose
participle names a feeling, filtered by WordNet's most frequent sense, by the
Lancaster Sensorimotor Norms above (dominant interoception) and by reviewed
inclusion and exclusion lists (scripts/build-emotion-lexicon.py).
nominalizations.tsv, modified by writemorebetter: noun-verb pairs from WordNet's
noun-to-verb derivational pointers, for single-word -tion, -sion, -ment, -ance,
-ence, -al and -ure nouns formed from the verb's stem, in the noun.act,
noun.cognition, noun.communication, noun.event, noun.process and noun.state
files, filtered by sense rank and SemCor tag counts, minus a reviewed exclusion
list and the nouns of emotions.tsv (scripts/build-hidden-verbs.py). Princeton
asks that WordNet be cited as: George A. Miller (1995). WordNet: A Lexical
Database for English. Communications of the ACM, 38(11), 39-41; and Christiane
Fellbaum (1998, ed.). WordNet: An Electronic Lexical Database. Cambridge, MA:
MIT Press. Princeton University does not endorse writemorebetter.

